IMPORT prelude

-- International Finance Corporation Act 1968 (Singapore) -- which payments to the Corporation are charged on the Consolidated Fund
-- (s 4) and the Minister's power to borrow for them (s 5); and the parts of Article VI of the Agreement that s 7(1) gives the force of
-- law, as a person dealing with the Corporation meets them: who may sue the Corporation and where (Article VI, section 3), seizure of
-- its property (sections 3 and 4), the immunities of its personnel (section 8), taxation of the Corporation, of its staff's salaries
-- and of its securities (section 9) with the s 7(1) proviso, and waiver (section 11).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IFCA1968.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The body carries no amendment
-- annotations; the Legislative History (not part of the Act) lists as its latest amending Act the Statutes (Miscellaneous
-- Amendments) Act 1991 (Act 11 of 1991, commencement 30 November 1991), followed by the 2013 Revised Edition.
-- The Schedule reproduces sections 2 to 9 and 11 of Article VI; sections 1 and 10 are not in the deposit.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0178 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. For a person, the answer is mostly the Schedule: whether and where they can sue the Corporation, whether its
-- officials can be sued, whether their Corporation salary or Corporation bond interest can be taxed. Not encoded: acceptance of the
-- Agreement (s 3), receipts (s 6, one sentence: sums received from the Corporation go into the Consolidated Fund), the Minister's
-- powers to amend the Schedule and make rules (ss 7(2), 8), Article VI sections 2, 5, 6 and 7 (stated in comments only), and the
-- Agreement itself beyond the Schedule (not deposited).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `International Finance Corporation Act 1968 -- immunities and payments`

§§ `4, 5 -- payments to the Corporation and borrowing for them`

-- s 4: "There shall be charged and paid out of the Consolidated Fund all sums required for the purpose of making payments on behalf of
-- the Government -- (a) under section 3 of Article II of the Agreement (which provides for the subscription of shares of stock of the
-- Corporation); and (b) under section 4 of Article V of the Agreement (which relates to the cessation of membership of the
-- Corporation)."
-- s 5: "For the purposes of providing any sums required for making any payments to the Corporation, the Minister with the President's
-- concurrence under Article 144(1)(b) of the Constitution may, on behalf of the Government, raise loans by the creation and issue of
-- securities"; their principal, interest and issue expenses are charged on the Consolidated Fund.
DECLARE Payment IS ONE OF
    `a subscription for shares under Article II section 3`
    `a payment on ceasing to be a member under Article V section 4`
    `some other payment to the Corporation`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4 charges the payment on the Consolidated Fund` IF
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `a subscription for shares under Article II section 3` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a payment on ceasing to be a member under Article V section 4` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the loan is to provide sums for payments to the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `the President concurs under Article 144(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may raise the loan under s 5` IF
        `the loan is to provide sums for payments to the Corporation`
    AND `the President concurs under Article 144(1)(b)`

§§ `Schedule, Article VI section 3 -- suing the Corporation`

-- Art VI s 2: the Corporation has "full juridical personality" and capacity to contract, to acquire and dispose of property and "to
-- institute legal proceedings".
-- Art VI s 3: "Actions may be brought against the Corporation only in a court of competent jurisdiction in the territories of a member
-- in which the Corporation has an office, has appointed an agent for the purpose of accepting service or notice of process, or has
-- issued or guaranteed securities. No actions shall, however, be brought by members or persons acting for or deriving claims from
-- members."
-- Unlike some other development-bank Schedules, there is no general immunity from legal process limited to borrowing or securities
-- claims: the restriction is on WHERE, and on WHO (members), not on WHAT the claim is about. The claim type is therefore a parameter
-- that changes nothing; the tests say so.
-- INFERENCE: section 11's waiver of "privileges and immunities" is not applied to section 3's venue condition or to the bar on members,
-- both of which are worded as limits on actions rather than as immunities. The text does not settle this.
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a claim on the Corporation's borrowing`
    `a claim on a Corporation guarantee`
    `a supplier's claim for the price of goods`
    `an employee's claim for wages`
    `a claim for personal injury on Corporation premises`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim,
      `the claimant is a member or acts for or derives a claim from a member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Corporation has an office, agent or issued or guaranteed securities in that member's territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action may be brought against the Corporation` IF
        (NOT `the claimant is a member or acts for or derives a claim from a member`)
    AND `the Corporation has an office, agent or issued or guaranteed securities in that member's territory`

§§ `Schedule, Article VI sections 3, 4 and 11 -- seizing the Corporation's property`

-- Art VI s 3: property and assets "shall, wheresoever located and by whomsoever held, be immune from all forms of seizure, attachment
-- or execution before the delivery of final judgment against the Corporation".
-- Art VI s 4: they "shall be immune from search, requisition, confiscation, expropriation or any other form of seizure by executive or
-- legislative action".
-- Art VI s 11: "The Corporation in its discretion may waive any of the privileges and immunities conferred under this Article to such
-- extent and upon such conditions as it may determine." Modelled as a whole waiver of the immunity in question (an inference: the text
-- allows partial and conditional waivers, which this boolean does not capture).
-- Art VI s 5 (archives inviolable), s 6 (assets free from restrictions, controls and moratoria "to the extent necessary"), s 7
-- (official communications treated as other members' are) are not encoded.
GIVEN `final judgment has been delivered against the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the taking is by executive or legislative action` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Corporation has waived the immunity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation's property may be seized` IF
        (`final judgment has been delivered against the Corporation` OR `the Corporation has waived the immunity`)
    AND ((NOT `the taking is by executive or legislative action`) OR `the Corporation has waived the immunity`)

§§ `Schedule, Article VI section 8 -- Corporation personnel`

-- Art VI s 8: "All Governors, Directors, Alternates, officers and employees of the Corporation -- (i) shall be immune from legal process
-- with respect to acts performed by them in their official capacity; (ii) not being local nationals, shall be accorded the same
-- immunities from immigration restrictions, alien registration requirements and national service obligations and the same facilities
-- as regards exchange restrictions as are accorded by members to the representatives, officials, and employees of comparable rank of
-- other members; (iii) shall be granted the same treatment in respect of travelling facilities".
-- Experts on missions are NOT named; nor is a contractor. Section 8(i) carries no waiver words of its own; the section 11 waiver is
-- applied to it.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `a Governor`
    `a Director`
    `an Alternate`
    `an officer`
    `an employee`
    `a consultant on a Corporation mission`
    `a contractor supplying the Corporation`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is section 8 personnel` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a consultant on a Corporation mission` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a contractor supplying the Corporation` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the act was in official capacity` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Corporation has waived the personal immunity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is immune from legal process for the act` IF
        `the person is section 8 personnel` `the person`
    AND `the act was in official capacity`
    AND (NOT `the Corporation has waived the personal immunity`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the person is a local national` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person gets the immigration and national service immunities` IF
        `the person is section 8 personnel` `the person`
    AND (NOT `the person is a local national`)

§§ `Schedule, Article VI section 9(a) and s 7(1) proviso -- taxation of the Corporation`

-- Art VI s 9(a): "The Corporation, its assets, property, income and its operations and transactions authorised by this Agreement, shall
-- be immune from all taxation and from all customs duties. The Corporation shall also be immune from liability for the collection or
-- payment of any tax or duty."
-- s 7(1) proviso: nothing in section 9 of Article VI shall be construed as "(a) entitling the Corporation to import into Singapore goods
-- free of any duty of customs without any restriction on their subsequent sale therein; (b) conferring on the Corporation any exemption
-- from taxes or duties which form part of the price of goods sold; or (c) conferring on the Corporation any exemption from taxes or
-- duties which are no more than charges for services rendered."
-- The "resale restricted" import is read from (a): duty-free import is not excluded where the later sale IS restricted (inference from
-- the words "without any restriction"). A duty to withhold tax is read as "liability for the collection" of tax (inference).
DECLARE Levy IS ONE OF
    `income tax on the Corporation's income`
    `customs duty on goods imported with a restriction on resale`
    `customs duty on goods imported with no restriction on resale`
    `a tax forming part of the price of goods sold to the Corporation`
    `a charge for services rendered`
    `a duty to withhold tax from the Corporation's payments`
    `a tax on the Corporation's authorised transactions`

GIVEN `the levy` IS A Levy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation is immune from the levy` IF
    CONSIDER `the levy`
    WHEN `customs duty on goods imported with no restriction on resale` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a tax forming part of the price of goods sold to the Corporation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a charge for services rendered` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Schedule, Article VI section 9(b) -- salaries paid by the Corporation`

-- Art VI s 9(b): "No tax shall be levied on or in respect of salaries and emoluments paid by the Corporation to Directors, Alternates,
-- officials or employees of the Corporation who are not local citizens, local subjects, or other local nationals."
-- Governors are named in section 8 but NOT in section 9(b). "Officials" is read as covering officers (inference). The exemption is lost
-- by being a local national; there is no member declaration to make, unlike the Asian Development Bank's Article 56(2).
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is named in section 9(b)` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a Governor` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a consultant on a Corporation mission` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a contractor supplying the Corporation` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the person is a local citizen, subject or national` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(b) bars tax on the Corporation salary` IF
        `the person is named in section 9(b)` `the person`
    AND (NOT `the person is a local citizen, subject or national`)

§§ `Schedule, Article VI section 9(c), (d) -- Corporation securities`

-- Art VI s 9(c): no taxation "of any kind" on any obligation or security ISSUED by the Corporation "(including any dividend or interest
-- thereon) by whomsoever held -- (i) which discriminates against such obligation or security solely because it is issued by the
-- Corporation; or (ii) if the sole jurisdictional basis for such taxation is the place or currency in which it is issued, made payable
-- or paid, or the location of any office or place of business maintained by the Corporation."
-- Art VI s 9(d): the same for a security GUARANTEED by the Corporation, but (ii) names only "the location of any office or place of
-- business maintained by the Corporation" -- not the place or currency of issue or payment.
DECLARE Basis IS ONE OF
    `the holder's residence`
    `the place of issue`
    `the currency of issue`
    `the place of payment`
    `the location of a Corporation office`

GIVEN `the basis` IS A Basis, `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the basis is a forbidden sole basis` IF
    CONSIDER `the basis`
    WHEN `the location of a Corporation office` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the place of issue` THEN `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Corporation`
    WHEN `the currency of issue` THEN `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Corporation`
    WHEN `the place of payment` THEN `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the basis` IS A Basis,
      `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the basis is the sole jurisdictional basis` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the tax discriminates solely because of the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9 bars the tax on the security` IF
        `the tax discriminates solely because of the Corporation`
    OR  (`the basis is the sole jurisdictional basis` AND `the basis is a forbidden sole basis` `the basis` `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Corporation`)
